#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059716 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059530 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c45a70b-273c-5fec-a768-40a1cf218628" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "65198cdd-dd3b-5840-aaf3-cecd96eb9d3b" :question/math-academy-id "e-4301" :question/problem "Let $\\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix}$ and $\\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$ Find a unit vector that is parallel to $\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{a + 2b}{\\mid a + 2b \\mid}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\na + 2b &= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + 2 \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}1 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 \\\\ 0\\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix}2 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}-2 + 2 \\\\ 0 + (-2)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\mid a + 2b \\mid &= \\sqrt{0^{2} + (-2)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{4} \\\\\n&= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $\\mathbf{a}+2\\mathbf{b}$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{a + 2b}{\\mid a + 2b \\mid} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2}(a + 2b) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c45a70b-273c-5fec-a768-40a1cf218628" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049360}] :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501451 :question-generator/id #uuid "a6ed5ab4-bef3-58f7-b4f0-03ce29d35739" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/