of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|2a+b| &= \\sqrt{(-12)^2+(-5)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{169} \\\\\n&= 13\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $2a+b$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{13}\\cdot (2a+b) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{13}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}-12 \\\\ -5\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}- \\frac{12}{13} \\\\ - \\frac{5}{13}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186501437 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9c45a70b-273c-5fec-a768-40a1cf218628" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "135f6880-f2d4-57f4-b6c2-f57d76de9846" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{9}{41} \\\\ \\frac{40}{123}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501418} {:answer/id #uuid "64d9579b-9034-5d26-9564-05a7d8dfa32d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 40\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501430} {:answer/id #uuid "71a98ba4-87aa-5cfb-85c6-16c3b6494b24" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{9}{41} \\\\ - \\frac{40}{41}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501433} {:answer/id #uuid "bc8348aa-d847-507f-b28b-29a3f3e30499" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{9}{82} \\\\ \\frac{40}{41}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501445} {:answer/id #uuid "c52d8eab-2ff9-5a8e-b72b-8b924b645da0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{9}{41} \\\\ \\frac{40}{41}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501446}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c52d8eab-2ff9-5a8e-b72b-8b924b645da0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{9}{41} \\\\ \\frac{40}{41}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501446} :answer-field/id #uuid "449fcc00-8553-5455-8f81-e7253900c6b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186501427}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "9375cd18-2a95-552f-b85a-1ce8d0584d8e" :question/problem "Let $a=\\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}$ and $b=\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 38\\end{bmatrix}$. Find a unit vector that is parallel to $2a+b$ and points the same direction." :question/requires-calculator false :question/worked-solution "Remember that to find a unit vector that is parallel to a given vector and points the same direction, we need to divide the given vector by its length:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|}\n$$\n\nFirst, let's compute the sum:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2a+b &= 2\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 1\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 38\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 38\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}0+(9) \\\\ (2)+(38)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 40\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUsing the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|2a+b| &= \\sqrt{(9)^2+(40)^2} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{1681} \\\\\n&= 41\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we divide $2a+b$ by its length and get the following unit vector:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nu &= \\frac{2a+b}{|2a+b|} \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{41}\\cdot (2a+b) \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{41}\\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}9 \\\\ 40\\end{bmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{9}{41} \\\\ \\frac{40}{41}\\end{bmatrix}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Unit Vector Parallel to a Given Vector"}]}
